00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.131
SPEAKER: With almost 500
sessions at Next 2018,

00:00:02.131 --> 00:00:04.380
it's understandable that you
couldn't get to them all.

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:06.588
So if you didn't see
Intelligent Internet of Things--

00:00:06.588 --> 00:00:08.740
Google Cloud's IoT
Vision, then stay tuned,

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:11.580
because here's the rewind.

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:13.980
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:18.090
By now you've probably heard--

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:19.830
IoT is a big deal.

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:21.580
Last year, the number
of connected devices

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:23.440
passed the population
of the planet.

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:27.400
This year, it's forecasted
to be up 27% over last year.

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:30.460
If these trends continue,
by 2025 IoT worldwide

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:33.820
will be generating 40
zettabytes of data.

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:34.750
What's a zettabyte?

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:36.460
It's a billion terabytes.

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:39.190
So while IoT is awesome, it's
becoming increasingly clear

00:00:39.190 --> 00:00:41.620
that IoT on its own isn't
the be all, end all.

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:43.390
We need smarts, we
need infrastructure

00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:45.640
around all of this
IoT data in order

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:48.400
to pull value out of
this glut that we've got.

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:49.960
This is where Google steps in.

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:52.060
As an industry leader in
artificial intelligence

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:54.220
and machine learning,
we have the platform

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:56.650
to make sense of this
mountain of data.

00:00:56.650 --> 00:00:59.320
While there's no agreement on
hardware, protocols, technology

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:01.479
stacks, we see some
common themes around IoT

00:01:01.479 --> 00:01:03.520
that we're going to be
pursuing through this year

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:04.780
and into the next.

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:06.490
I want to touch on a couple.

00:01:06.490 --> 00:01:08.170
The big announcement
from Cloud Next

00:01:08.170 --> 00:01:09.922
is that we've developed
a new product that

00:01:09.922 --> 00:01:11.380
will push the
boundaries of putting

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:13.480
that intelligence everywhere.

00:01:13.480 --> 00:01:16.270
Cloud IoT Edge extends
Google Cloud's powerful data

00:01:16.270 --> 00:01:19.780
processing and machine learning
to billions of Edge devices,

00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:23.080
such as robotic arms, wind
turbines, oil rigs, smart cars,

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:25.330
cameras, so they can
all act on the data

00:01:25.330 --> 00:01:29.034
from their sensors in real time
and predict outcomes locally.

00:01:29.034 --> 00:01:31.450
We didn't stop at developing
this awesome runtime, though.

00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:34.870
We also announced our Edge TPU,
Google's purpose-built hardware

00:01:34.870 --> 00:01:37.210
accelerator chip that
enables lightning speed

00:01:37.210 --> 00:01:38.737
inferences on the Edge.

00:01:38.737 --> 00:01:41.320
All of this running on a secure
and managed operating system--

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:44.530
Android Things-- and
soon on Linux OS as well.

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:47.680
We're making our Cloud IoT
platform serverless by design,

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:50.590
so that you can go from proof
to concept with hundreds

00:01:50.590 --> 00:01:53.980
of devices to productions with
millions of devices in days,

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:55.960
while keeping it
entirely modular.

00:01:55.960 --> 00:01:59.860
Cloud IoT Core, our IoT
gateway, is critical here.

00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:02.350
To touch on just a couple of
things with our IoT Core--

00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:03.280
provisioning.

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:05.050
Millions of devices
can be connected

00:02:05.050 --> 00:02:08.259
to Cloud IoT Core with zero
provisioning operations.

00:02:08.259 --> 00:02:10.419
We're working with select
secure element vendors

00:02:10.419 --> 00:02:11.710
to make this possible.

00:02:11.710 --> 00:02:13.900
High-speed, scalable
messaging-- it

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:15.809
will make control
scenarios much easier

00:02:15.809 --> 00:02:17.350
where you want to
be able to directly

00:02:17.350 --> 00:02:20.110
influence the state of your
devices from the cloud.

00:02:20.110 --> 00:02:22.270
Support for gateway
devices to represent

00:02:22.270 --> 00:02:25.780
a multitude of less powerful or
less secure on-premise sensors.

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:27.610
All these features
being added to IoT Core

00:02:27.610 --> 00:02:30.400
represent a more robust scaling.

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:31.979
We've already in
past conversations

00:02:31.979 --> 00:02:34.270
talked quite a bit about how
Google's infrastructure is

00:02:34.270 --> 00:02:36.570
built for security
from the ground up.

00:02:36.570 --> 00:02:39.040
IoT Core has continued that
trend with solid security

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:42.220
in place, using TLS to encrypt
communication and JSON web

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:43.349
tokens for authentication.

00:02:43.349 --> 00:02:45.640
I want to call out something
that we announced at Next.

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:47.740
Our partners over at
Microchip have come up

00:02:47.740 --> 00:02:51.460
with an 8-bit MCU that provides
a hardware route of trust

00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:54.520
to securely connect over
Wi-Fi to Cloud IoT Core.

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:57.190
Being able to connect an 8-bit
chip securely to the cloud

00:02:57.190 --> 00:03:00.130
will change the landscape
of connected devices.

00:03:00.130 --> 00:03:02.286
And lastly, I couldn't
talk about Google's vision

00:03:02.286 --> 00:03:04.660
for IoT and the cloud without
mentioning all the partners

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:05.800
that we work with.

00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:09.080
As big as Google is, we won't
ever have all the answers.

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:10.750
We rely on these
amazing companies

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:13.360
to blend their technologies
with our cloud functionality

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:15.970
to create solutions that
solve the world's problems one

00:03:15.970 --> 00:03:17.439
device at a time.

00:03:17.439 --> 00:03:19.480
As well as working with
all these great partners,

00:03:19.480 --> 00:03:22.210
at the end of May, we announced
that Google's joining the LoRa

00:03:22.210 --> 00:03:24.584
Alliance, and we're committed
to working with our partner

00:03:24.584 --> 00:03:26.962
network to nurture this
ecosystem together.

00:03:26.962 --> 00:03:28.420
If you'd like to
see the full talk,

00:03:28.420 --> 00:03:30.260
check out the link in
the description below.

00:03:30.260 --> 00:03:32.343
And don't forget to subscribe
to the Cloud YouTube

00:03:32.343 --> 00:03:34.280
channel for more great
Next Rewind content.

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:35.113
Thanks for watching.

